<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">As of December 31, 2022 and
June 30, 2023, all accounts receivable was due from third party customers. Provision for credit losses for the year ended December 31,
2022 and the six months ended June 30, 2023 was RMB<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c52" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProvisionForOtherCreditLosses" scale="3" unitRef="cny">861</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c0" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProvisionForOtherCreditLosses" scale="3" unitRef="cny">8,593</ix:nonFraction>.</p><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&#160;</p></ix:nonNumeric><div>
</div><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"></p><div>

